1
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:12,080
Someone says: a square is a rectangle, and a rectangle is a parallelogram.

2
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:13,520
Is that true?

3
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:15,180
Is a square a rectangle?

4
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:18,460
Pause the video and decide.

5
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:22,260
A rectangle is any quadrilateral with 4 right angles.

6
00:00:22,310 --> 00:00:27,220
A square has 4 right angles, so yes, a square is a special rectangle.

7
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:29,630
It also has 4 equal sides.

8
00:00:29,680 --> 00:00:36,610
Remember: a regular polygon with n sides has n lines of symmetry, and rotational symmetry of order n.

9
00:00:36,660 --> 00:00:40,070
A regular octagon has 8 lines of symmetry.

10
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:46,110
Each quadrilateral has its own properties: sides, angles, diagonals and symmetry.

11
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:48,360
Look carefully at the diagonals.

12
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:55,240
In a kite, the diagonals cross at 90 degrees, but only one of them cuts the other in half.

13
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:55,960
Your turn.

14
00:00:56,010 --> 00:01:00,680
The diagonals cross at 90 degrees, and only one bisects the other.

15
00:01:00,730 --> 00:01:01,970
Which shape is it?

16
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:05,300
Pause the video and choose.

17
00:01:05,350 --> 00:01:06,210
It is a kite.

18
00:01:06,260 --> 00:01:10,390
The long diagonal cuts the short one in half, at 90 degrees.

19
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,560
But the short one does not cut the long one in half.

20
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:19,430
A shape belongs to a family if it has all the properties of that family.

21
00:01:19,480 --> 00:01:26,410
So a square is a rectangle, a rectangle is a parallelogram, and a parallelogram is a trapezium.

22
00:01:26,460 --> 00:01:30,540
A square is also a rhombus, and a rhombus is a parallelogram.

23
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,780
A rhombus is also a kite.

24
00:01:32,830 --> 00:01:35,100
But not every rhombus is a square.

25
00:01:35,150 --> 00:01:38,180
A rhombus does not need right angles.

26
00:01:38,230 --> 00:01:39,520
Here is the method.

27
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:41,210
Step 1: check the sides.

28
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:42,270
Are they equal?

29
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,090
Are they parallel?

30
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:45,880
Step 2: check the angles.

31
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:46,810
Right angles?

32
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,930
Opposite angles equal?

33
00:01:48,980 --> 00:01:51,010
Step 3: check the diagonals.

34
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:51,450
Equal?

35
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:52,490
Perpendicular?

36
00:01:52,540 --> 00:01:54,970
Do they bisect each other?

37
00:01:55,020 --> 00:01:57,610
Step 4: name the most specific shape.

38
00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:01,790
But remember it belongs to the bigger families too.

39
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:08,140
A quadrilateral's diagonals are equal and bisect each other, but they are not perpendicular.

40
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:09,250
Name it.

41
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:12,190
Bisecting diagonals means a parallelogram.

42
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:14,580
Equal diagonals means a rectangle.

43
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:17,600
Not perpendicular means it is not a square.

44
00:02:17,650 --> 00:02:19,620
So it is a rectangle.

45
00:02:19,670 --> 00:02:23,320
A rhombus has 2 lines of symmetry: its two diagonals.

46
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:29,170
It looks the same after a half turn, so its rotational symmetry has order 2.

47
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:29,870
Your turn.

48
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:34,070
What is the order of rotational symmetry of a parallelogram?

49
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:37,010
Pause and work it out.

50
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:42,030
A parallelogram fits onto itself after a half turn, and after a full turn.

51
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,250
So the order is 2.

52
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:45,970
But it has no lines of symmetry.

53
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:49,760
True or false: a trapezium can have a line of symmetry.

54
00:02:49,810 --> 00:02:50,100
True.

55
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:56,090
An isosceles trapezium has one line, through the middles of the parallel sides.

56
00:02:56,140 --> 00:02:59,270
A shape has exactly one pair of parallel sides.

57
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,150
Ben names it.

58
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:02,060
Which line is wrong?

59
00:03:02,110 --> 00:03:03,190
Line 2 is wrong.

60
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:06,750
A parallelogram needs two pairs of parallel sides.

61
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,210
One pair makes a trapezium.

62
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:11,780
The shape is a trapezium.

63
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:15,160
Many folding tables and lamps use parallelograms.

64
00:03:15,210 --> 00:03:22,970
When the sides are joined at hinges, a parallelogram can lean over, but its opposite sides stay parallel.

65
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:26,550
So the table top stays level, even as the legs fold.

66
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:30,690
A rectangle that leans over becomes a parallelogram.

67
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:31,920
One last question.

68
00:03:31,970 --> 00:03:34,880
A rhombus with a right angle is what shape?

69
00:03:34,930 --> 00:03:38,140
Pause the video and choose.

70
00:03:38,190 --> 00:03:40,180
A rhombus has 4 equal sides.

71
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:45,090
If one angle is 90 degrees, all four are, so it is a square.

72
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:51,360
To remember: know the sides, angles, diagonals and symmetry of each quadrilateral.

73
00:03:51,410 --> 00:03:55,410
A square is a rectangle, and a rectangle is a parallelogram.

74
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:57,790
A square is also a rhombus.

75
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:02,830
A regular polygon with n sides has n lines of symmetry, and order n.

76
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,020
Name the most specific shape that fits.

77
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:11,190
Great work! Now practise lesson 8.1 on Camday.
